.TH DANBY-SOFTBALLPITCH 1
.SH NAME
danby-softballpitch \- drag and spin on a pitched softball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/softballpitch
.SH MODEL
This model uses the same velocity-squared drag and Magnus-force equations as
the baseball model, with a lower release height, speed, and coefficients suited
to the larger ball.  It follows the pitch for 0.8 seconds or to ground impact.
.SH DISPLAY
The plots show height against distance and speed against time.  Tracks alter
speed, angle, drag, lift, spin, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/softballpitch.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
